hortened code and after encoding, these zero bytes are removed. The punctured code is then generated for which specific parity symbols are discarded from the output of the encoder.\n\n### 1.2.3. Convolutional Encoder\n\nThe RS output code-word is fed to inner binary convolutional encoder that has ½ coding rate and 7 constraint length as shown in Fig. (4). The generator polynomial is determined by G1= 171 OCT for X and G2= 133 OCT for Y.\n\nBy puncturing operation, different code rate can be obtained from the output of convolutional encoder. In the standard, three different code rate can be achieved 2/3, 3/4 and 5/6.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRL78 Family Microcontrollers Brochure (https://www.renesas.com/en/document/bro/rl78-family-brochure?language=en&r=1168926)\nciteturn0search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: 11 months ago; – DALI-2 communication H/W support ... - Debug (Single Wire, Two Wires) ... - RAM Parity Check ... - True Random Number Generator\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\n\n## Block Diagram\n\nFunctional block architecture of the RL78/G24.\n\n**FAA Core**\n- Flexible Application Accelerator\n\n**RL78 CPU Core**\n- 48 MHz 76.8 DMIPS\n- CISC Harvard Architecture, 3-stage Pipeline\n- Four-Register Banks\n- 16-bit Barrel Shifter\n\n**Memory**\n- Program Flash up to 128KB\n- SRAM up to 12KB\n- Data Flash 4KB\n\n**System**\n- Interrupt Controller, 4 Levels\n- POR, LVD\n- Clock Generation (Internal, External)\n- Data Transfer Controller\n- Event Link Controller\n- Debug (Single Wire, Two Wires)\n- PLL\n\n**Power Management**\n- HALT — ADC, DAC, RTC Enabled\n- SNOOZE — DTC, ADC Enabled\n- STOP — RTC Enabled\n\n**Human Machine Interface**\n- Output Current Control Port, 8ch\n\n**Safety**\n- RAM Parity Check\n- ADC Self-diagnostic\n- Clock Monitoring\n- Memory CRC\n- Output Level Detection\n\n**Communication**\n- IICA, 1ch\n- IICA (SM/PM bus), 1ch\n- LIN, 1ch\n- DALI, 1ch\n\n**Security & Encryption**\n- Flash Read Protection\n- Flash Shield Protection\n- Unique ID\n- Customer ID\n- True Random Number Generator\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSumsets and entropy revisited (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/rsa.21252)\nciteturn0search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.3 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Conjecture 1.7. ... Prior to this paper, the best known bound in the direction of this conjecture was a result of the second author [14].\nSuch stronger statements are also speculated to be true, but care must be taken in their formulation, as discussed in [13].)\n\nConjecture 1.7. (Weak PFR over $$$ \\mathbf{Z} $$$)Suppose that $$$ A\\subseteq {\\mathbf{Z}}^D $$$ is a set with $$$ \\sigma \\left[A\\right]\\le K $$$. Then there is a subset $$$ {A}^{\\prime}\\subseteq A $$$, $$$ \\mid {A}^{\\prime}\\mid \\ge {K}^{-O(1)}\\mid A\\mid $$$, with $$$ \\dim {A}^{\\prime}\\ll \\log K $$$.\n\nPrior to this paper, the best known bound in the direction of this conjecture was a result of the second author [14].\n\nTheorem 1.8. ([[14], theorem 1.5])Suppose that $$$ A\\subseteq {\\mathbf{Z}}^D $$$ is a finite set with $$$ \\sigma \\left[A\\right]\\le K $$$. Then there is $$$ {A}^{\\prime}\\subseteq A $$$ with $$$ \\frac{\\mid {A}^{\\prime}\\mid }{\\mid A\\mid}\\gg \\exp \\left(-C{\\log}^2K\\right) $$$ and $$$ \\dim {A}^{\\prime}\\ll \\log K $$$.\n\nThe proof of this result in [14] was a little exotic, making use of projections modulo 2 and a kind of “$$$ {U}^3 $$$-energy”. We provide a new, shorter, proof of this result, retaining the first feature but using entropic notions in place of the exotic energy.\n\nWe will eventually go further in this paper by using results on sets with additive structure in $$$ {\\mathbf{F}}_2^D $$$ to improve the bounds, but before doing that we make a detour into the world of structure theorems for sets of small doubling in $$$ {\\mathbf{F}}_2^D $$$.\n\n-------------------------